{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":116955,"name":"Mateusz Sadowski","username":"msadowski","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/msadowski/{size}/33950_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-18T17:15:01.231Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt Foxglove, we announced quite a few new features today and wanted to share them with the community. Here is what we’ve been cooking:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116955-search-experience-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116955-search-experience-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSearch Experience\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can query all your recordings in Foxglove and quickly get to the data you need. The example query I always demo is: `\u003ccode\u003e/mti/imu/linear_acceleration.x \u0026gt; 11\u003c/code\u003e`. It gets more exciting as of Today, because you can combine the topic search with semantic search, and for example run the following query: `\u003ccode\u003evisual(\"stairs\") AND (/anymal/imu/linear_acceleration.x \u0026gt; 4 OR /anymal/imu/linear_acceleration.x \u0026lt; -4)\u003c/code\u003e` gets me a good set of instances of my robot walking on stairs to work with:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/0/8/0887a80c82de8f6cba8fe04056359617cf8671b0.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/1dssFgqv7Bw8X9fWThhBzZMBlwA.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"visual-acc-search\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0887a80c82de8f6cba8fe04056359617cf8671b0_2_690x396.jpeg\" alt=\"visual-acc-search\" data-base62-sha1=\"1dssFgqv7Bw8X9fWThhBzZMBlwA\" width=\"690\" height=\"396\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0887a80c82de8f6cba8fe04056359617cf8671b0_2_690x396.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0887a80c82de8f6cba8fe04056359617cf8671b0_2_1035x594.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0887a80c82de8f6cba8fe04056359617cf8671b0_2_1380x792.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"3F4147\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003evisual-acc-search\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1920×1103 331 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd, of course, if you click any of these results, you’ll see the exact moment and can start working with the data immediately.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://foxglove.dev/blog/introducing-semantic-search\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eLearn more\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116955-ab-comparison-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116955-ab-comparison-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eA/B Comparison\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can now easily compare two or more runs in Foxglove. Load the bag files, align the time offsets, and visualize the two runs on the same timeline. Here is one example of running a UMBMark test and visualizing odometry before and after calibration:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/c/e/ce13df8cdc612403358f7a7d3b5c7ac7b334acd1.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/tp2W6mAjxE0MH4jKIo6WX1FTqRr.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"ab-umb-mark-demo\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/e/ce13df8cdc612403358f7a7d3b5c7ac7b334acd1_2_690x365.jpeg\" alt=\"ab-umb-mark-demo\" data-base62-sha1=\"tp2W6mAjxE0MH4jKIo6WX1FTqRr\" width=\"690\" height=\"365\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/e/ce13df8cdc612403358f7a7d3b5c7ac7b334acd1_2_690x365.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/e/ce13df8cdc612403358f7a7d3b5c7ac7b334acd1_2_1035x547.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/e/ce13df8cdc612403358f7a7d3b5c7ac7b334acd1_2_1380x730.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"1B2227\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eab-umb-mark-demo\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1920×1018 206 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVideo of the example above: \u003ca href=\"https://youtu.be/wdSkFHLtZwU\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://youtu.be/wdSkFHLtZwU\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://foxglove.dev/blog/compare-robot-recordings-across-runs\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eLearn more\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116955-agent-sidebar-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116955-agent-sidebar-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAgent Sidebar\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe have an agent sidebar now. You can ask the agent to create layouts for you, help you triage issues, write userscripts, create events, and more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/3/a/3ade8f9b05c0bb61a9de5f739f374e60ebcaf28e.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/8oMwJpmrBmNW9TjNiVhZX8JoSuy.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"new-chat-create-layout\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/3/a/3ade8f9b05c0bb61a9de5f739f374e60ebcaf28e_2_690x395.jpeg\" alt=\"new-chat-create-layout\" data-base62-sha1=\"8oMwJpmrBmNW9TjNiVhZX8JoSuy\" width=\"690\" height=\"395\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/3/a/3ade8f9b05c0bb61a9de5f739f374e60ebcaf28e_2_690x395.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/3/a/3ade8f9b05c0bb61a9de5f739f374e60ebcaf28e_2_1035x592.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/3/a/3ade8f9b05c0bb61a9de5f739f374e60ebcaf28e_2_1380x790.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"303438\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003enew-chat-create-layout\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1920×1101 298 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe also have an MCP in the desktop app, so you can connect your agent of choice to Foxglove and ask it to do things for you. My favorite prompt so far was asking it to triage an issue and create a PDF report for my boss.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://foxglove.dev/blog/foxglove-goes-agentic\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eLearn more\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116955-remote-access-and-byos-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116955-remote-access-and-byos-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRemote Access and BYOS\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis and the next feature are not agent-related, but I thought I would mention them since I have your attention. With Bring Your Own Server (BYOS), you use your own storage bucket with Foxglove (no longer need to keep two separate copies of your data).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRemote Access enables a connection to your robot through an optimized WebRTC stream, where we optimize stream quality based on the available bandwidth.\u003cbr\u003e\nRead more:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://foxglove.dev/blog/remote-access-is-generally-available\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRemote Access blog post\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://foxglove.dev/blog/bring-your-own-storage-is-generally-available\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eBYOS blog post\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you have any questions or feedback, don’t hesitate to let me know! If you happen to be at \u003ca href=\"https://actuate.foxglove.dev/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eActuate\u003c/a\u003e today or tomorrow, let me know, and let’s try to catch up!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-08-18T17:15:01.231Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":19,"reads":55,"readers_count":54,"score":166.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":57496,"topic_slug":"foxglove-has-agents-now","display_username":"Mateusz Sadowski","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://foxglove.dev/blog/remote-access-is-generally-available","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Remote Access is generally available | Foxglove","clicks":2},{"url":"https://youtu.be/wdSkFHLtZwU","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":2},{"url":"https://foxglove.dev/blog/bring-your-own-storage-is-generally-available","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Bring Your Own Storage is now available on all major clouds | Foxglove","clicks":1},{"url":"https://foxglove.dev/blog/introducing-semantic-search","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Introducing Semantic Search | Foxglove","clicks":1},{"url":"https://foxglove.dev/blog/compare-robot-recordings-across-runs","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Compare robot recordings across runs | Foxglove","clicks":1},{"url":"https://foxglove.dev/blog/foxglove-goes-agentic","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Foxglove goes agentic | Foxglove","clicks":0},{"url":"https://actuate.foxglove.dev/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Actuate 26 | Annual Robotics Developer Conference","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":13481,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/foxglove-has-agents-now/57496/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3},{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":4,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_vote":false},{"id":117058,"name":"Abderahmane BENALI","username":"benaliabderahmane","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/benaliabderahmane/{size}/16284_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-20T16:29:11.609Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/msadowski\"\u003e@msadowski\u003c/a\u003e, nice release\u003cbr\u003e\nA question on the agent side, I couldn’t find anything in the docs about data handling. What’s the retention policy for agent conversations and tool results, is there a zero-retention arrangement with the model provider, and is any of it used for training or eval?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-08-20T16:29:11.609Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":36,"readers_count":35,"score":7.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":57496,"topic_slug":"foxglove-has-agents-now","display_username":"Abderahmane BENALI","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":24869,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[{"id":13481,"username":"msadowski","name":"Mateusz Sadowski","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/msadowski/{size}/33950_2.png"}],"post_url":"/t/foxglove-has-agents-now/57496/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":117059,"name":"Martin Pecka","username":"peci1","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/peci1/{size}/10145_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-20T17:19:17.065Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSounds great! When does FG do the analysis for semantic search? Is it done somewhere in the cloud afrer you upload the bag?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-08-20T17:19:17.065Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":34,"readers_count":33,"score":6.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":57496,"topic_slug":"foxglove-has-agents-now","display_username":"Martin Pecka","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-news-for-the-week-of-august-17th-2026/57592","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"ROS News for the Week of August 17th, 2026","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Great contributor","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":5103,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"user_status":{"description":"Czech Technical University in Prague","emoji":"czechia","ends_at":null,"message_bus_last_id":0},"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/foxglove-has-agents-now/57496/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":117133,"name":"Mateusz Sadowski","username":"msadowski","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/msadowski/{size}/33950_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-21T21:16:04.744Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/benaliabderahmane\"\u003e@benaliabderahmane\u003c/a\u003e Thanks for the question! No data is used for training or eval. As for the retention policy, I’ll check with the team and try to get back to you.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/peci1\"\u003e@peci1\u003c/a\u003e Yes, you can enable search for certain topic patterns in image/video data and tell us how far back we should look for the first ingestion; then we’ll analyze the new data as it arrives and create the vector store for the embeddings, making it searchable.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-08-21T21:16:04.744Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"